  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Sun Shi Han lists him among Liu tribe’s strong experts beside Pei Yan Fei. Bei Cao Chuan then names him the current Chang tribe leader, once Chang Shan Yin’s best friend, who married that man’s wife after the disappearance and raised the young tribe leader Chang Ji You.",
      "chapters": [
        527
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_sun_shi_han",
        "fac_liu_tribe",
        "char_pei_yan_fei",
        "char_bei_cao_chuan",
        "fac_chang_tribe",
        "char_chang_shan_yin",
        "char_chang_ji_you"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the mirror Chang Biao has green-grey skin. Fangs grow out of his mouth. His eyes are yellow. He has green-red messy hair. Six monstrous arms of different shapes and sizes sit on his back, each ruthless looking.",
      "chapters": [
        577
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In Liu tribe camp he is Chang tribe’s current tribe leader, called Chang Shan Yin’s brother, and a rank four upper stage wind path expert. In private he tells Ni Xue Tong he plotted with Ha Tu Gu against Chang Shan Yin, then used brother status to marry her and make Chang Ji You his godson, and that this reputation helped him take the tribe leader seat.",
      "chapters": [
        530
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribe-leader-and-wind-path",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ni_xue_tong",
        "char_ha_tu_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan makes himself Chang tribe’s sole supreme elder, sets Chang Ji You as tribe leader, and keeps Chang Biao as number one elder while leaving Ni Xue Tong as Chang Biao’s wife.",
      "chapters": [
        536
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "elder-under-wolf-king",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later, with Pan Ping, he tests six arm heavenly zombie king and schemes a Wolf Killing Alliance against Wolf King while still serving as Chang tribe’s great elder under that arrangement.",
      "chapters": [
        576
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "elder-under-wolf-king",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_pan_ping",
        "fac_wolf_killing_alliance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the tower’s seventh floor ninetieth round he dies of exhaustion after heavy use of that killer move; Fang Yuan finds the corpse and names accumulated zombie energy as the main cause of death, and takes his wind path Gu worms.",
      "chapters": [
        580
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "elder-under-wolf-king",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "As he uses six arm heavenly zombie king more often, irrecoverable zombie speckles grow on his body and become denser.",
      "chapters": [
        580
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "zombie-speckles",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes the name as Chang Biao. No Chinese characters for the personal name appear in the English chapter text used here.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
